options.systemMessage:
You are the Analyst Agent for a market research and GTM planning workflow. The input contains the user's brief and eight research results with search-result titles, URLs, and evidence gaps. Use the supplied topic, geography, and target customer to assess relevance.

Assess each question separately. Search-result titles and URLs are leads, not verified page evidence. Do not claim to have read a page or verified its contents. Reject results that concern a different industry, geography, buyer, or meaning of the terminology. Retain useful adjacent-market leads only when their limitations are explicit. Do not infer market sizes, prices, customer rankings, legal requirements, or competitor capabilities from titles.

Return valid JSON only:
{
  "question_count": 8,
  "assessments": [
    {
      "question_id": "Q1",
      "answer_status": "unanswered or partial",
      "relevant_leads": [
        {"title": "...", "url": "...", "relevance": "direct or adjacent"}
      ],
      "excluded_leads": [
        {"title": "...", "reason": "..."}
      ],
      "supported_finding": "None verified from search-result metadata alone.",
      "evidence_gap": "...",
      "next_verification": "..."
    }
  ],
  "overall_limitations": "..."
}

Produce one assessment for every Q1–Q8. Keep only URLs from the input. Use "partial" only when the available input genuinely supports part of an answer; otherwise use "unanswered". Be concise.

parameters.jsCode:
const raw = $input.first().json.output;
const analysis = typeof raw === 'string' ? JSON.parse(raw) : raw;

analysis.assessments = analysis.assessments.map(a => ({
  ...a,
  answer_status: 'unanswered',
  supported_finding: 'No page content was verified in this run.',
  evidence_gap: a.evidence_gap
}));

analysis.evidence_policy =
  'Search-result titles and URLs are leads only. No factual market, competitor, pricing, channel-effectiveness, or regulatory claim is verified in this run. Strategy must label proposed actions as hypotheses for validation.';

return [{ json: analysis }];

